<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!-- keepawake has no window at all — the tray icon's right-click menu is the only surface this
         ever reaches. On Windows, that menu is a real Avalonia MenuItem/Flyout popup, not OS-native
         chrome (native menus are only genuinely OS-drawn on macOS/Linux — confirmed via Avalonia
         maintainer guidance in github.com/AvaloniaUI/Avalonia/discussions/8301: "if you want to style
         native tray menu on windows, just style MenuItem control").

         Targeting MenuItem directly, not TextBlock: SimpleTheme's MenuItem.xaml renders string headers
         through an AccessText (for the mnemonic underline), which *is* a TextBlock subclass, but a
         bare `Style Selector="TextBlock"` only matches the exact type in Avalonia, not subclasses (that
         needs `:is(TextBlock)`) — so a TextBlock-only selector silently never reaches it. FontFamily is
         an inherited property and MenuItem's own template never sets it locally, so setting it here on
         MenuItem itself flows down into that AccessText regardless of the type-matching subtlety. -->
    <Style Selector="MenuItem">
        <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{DynamicResource MartianMono}"/>
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource OnSurfaceBrush}"/>
    </Style>

</Styles>
